/surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Antigen presentation by chemically modified splenocytes induces antigen-specific T cell unresponsiveness in vitro and in vivo</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><year>1987</year><volume>165</volume><fpage>302</fpage><lpage>319</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3029267</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schwartz</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Models of T cell anergy: is there a  common molecular mechanism? </article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><year>1996</year><volume>184</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8691122</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sloan-Lancaster</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Evavold</surname><given-names>BD</given-names></name><name><surname>Allen</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Th2 cell clonal anergy as a consequence of partial activation</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><year>1994</year><volume>180</volume><fpage>1195</fpage><lpage>1205</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7931057</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Otten</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name><name><surname>Germain</surname><given-names>RN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Split anergy in a  CD8<sup>&#x0002b;</sup>T cell receptor&#x02013;dependent cytolysis in the absence of interleukin-2 production</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1991</year><volume>251</volume><fpage>1228</fpage><lpage>1231</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1900952</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label